cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use llm-json-doctor in research or in a product, please cite it as below."
title: "llm-json-doctor"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic, dependency-free repair and validation for malformed LLM JSON.
  Repairs fenced or prose-wrapped output, JSON5-style syntax, truncation and
  common model defects, logs every transformation as a machine-readable action,
  and applies a small schema-guided validation and coercion layer. Python 3.9+,
  standard library only, no model calls and no network at runtime.
authors:
  - name: "llm-json-doctor contributors"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Qin-Z-x/llm-json-doctor"
url: "https://github.com/Qin-Z-x/llm-json-doctor"
type: software
keywords:
  - "JSON repair"
  - "malformed JSON"
  - "LLM structured output"
  - "JSON Schema validation"
  - "deterministic parsing"
